        <body>
            <div xml:id="d607">

                <pb facs="1068" n="974" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg974"/>

                <head>No. 607.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Child to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-08-31"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 31, 1887</date>.
                        (Received October 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 40.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: It gives me pleasure to inclose a copy of
                    translation of a letter from his excellency Phya Bhaskarawongse, acting minister
                    for foreign flairs, in reply to a dispatch sent by me with extracts from your in
                    struction No. 18, diplomatic series, under date July 1, 1887, in regard to the
                    Siamese Government having left the United States put of the new law that is
                    shortly to go into operation relating to the importation and sale of liquors,
                    and in which he assures me that the proper correction has been made.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jaoob T. Child.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d607-a1.xml" xpointer="d607-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
